1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,484
You walk in, and you're

2
00:00:01,484 --> 00:00:02,760
sure everyone noticed.

3
00:00:03,210 --> 00:00:04,092
The stain.

4
00:00:04,342 --> 00:00:05,521
The awkward wave.

5
00:00:05,771 --> 00:00:06,849
The voice crack.

6
00:00:07,449 --> 00:00:08,600
But here's the thing:

7
00:00:08,750 --> 00:00:10,189
they almost certainly didn't.

8
00:00:10,889 --> 00:00:13,126
In 2000, Cornell psychologists

9
00:00:13,126 --> 00:00:14,990
sent students into a room

10
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:17,001
wearing a T-shirt with a cheesy

11
00:00:17,001 --> 00:00:18,321
pop star's face on it.

12
00:00:18,821 --> 00:00:20,027
Then they asked: how

13
00:00:20,027 --> 00:00:21,234
many people noticed?

14
00:00:21,834 --> 00:00:22,913
The students guessed

15
00:00:22,913 --> 00:00:23,993
about half the room.

16
00:00:24,393 --> 00:00:26,839
The real answer? About 1 in 4.

17
00:00:27,639 --> 00:00:28,480
It's called the

18
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:29,433
spotlight effect.

19
00:00:29,883 --> 00:00:31,306
You feel like you're on

20
00:00:31,306 --> 00:00:32,976
stage, under a giant light.

21
00:00:33,226 --> 00:00:34,287
But everyone else is

22
00:00:34,287 --> 00:00:35,720
starring in their own show,

23
00:00:35,870 --> 00:00:36,645
worrying about

24
00:00:36,645 --> 00:00:37,531
their own stain.

25
00:00:38,231 --> 00:00:40,032
So next time you feel watched,

26
00:00:40,232 --> 00:00:41,849
remember: you're the only one

27
00:00:41,849 --> 00:00:43,076
holding the spotlight.
